ouette_sculpture_of_Norsemen_above_L%27Anse_aux_Meadows%2C_NFL_CAN.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2022-08-27_04_Silhouette_sculpture_of_Norsemen_above_L%27Anse_aux_Meadows,_NFL_CAN.jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=154758645","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2024-11-05 18:20:36","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"2022-08-27 04 Silhouette sculpture of Norsemen above L'Anse aux Meadows, NFL CAN","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"L'Anse aux Meadows|Self-published work|Information field template with formatting|Heritage properties in Canada with known IDs|Images from Wiki Loves Monuments 2024|Uploaded via Campaign:wlm-ca|Images from Wiki Loves Monuments missing SDC source of file|Images from Wiki Loves Monuments 2024 in Canada|Norsemen silhouette sculpture","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"quality|featured|valued","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"GPSLatitude":{"value":"51.591853","source":"commons-desc-page"},"GPSLongitude":{"value":"-55.533518","source":"commons-desc-page"},"GPSMapDatum":{"value":"WGS-84","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"Norse silhouette sculpture above <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/L%27Anse_aux_Meadows\">L'Anse aux Meadows National Historic Site</a>, Newfoundland Canada on August 27, 2022.  \n<p>This sculpture commemorates the arrival of the Vikings in approximately 1021 and was designed by New Brunswick artist, Karen Van Niekerk. It is made of <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weathering_steel\">corten steel</a>, 10 millimeters thick and approximately 2.4 meters high, \n</p>\nMost of the Norse figures look southeast to symbolize their intent to use L\u2019Anse aux Meadows as a base camp to explore further southward from Newfoundland's Great Northern Peninsula. One looks back to southern Greenland from whence they came. There is a woman figure indicative of families that came during the period that L'Anse aux Meadows was used as a base camp.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2022-08-27 17:58:25","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<span class=\"int-own-work\" lang=\"en\">Own work</span>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:GRDN711\" title=\"User:GRDN711\">Gordon Leggett</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Permission":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Attribution":{"value":"Photo: <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User_talk:GRDN711\" title=\"User talk:GRDN711\">Gordon Leggett</a>\u00a0/\u00a0<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Main_Page\" title=\"Main Page\">Wikimedia Commons</a>","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Creative Commons Attribution-Share Alike 4.0","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"true","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"LicenseUrl":{"value":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Copyrighted":{"value":"True","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"cc-by-sa-4.0","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}}}]},"154822663":{"pageid":154822663,"ns":6,"title":"File:2022-08-28 06 Meeting of Two Worlds \u2013 Boykov \u2013 Brixel - L'Anse aux Meadows, NFL CAN.jpg","index":4,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/2022-08-28_06_Meeting_of_Two_Worlds_%E2%80%93_Boykov_%E2%80%93_Brixel_-_L%27Anse_aux_Meadows%2C_NFL_CAN.jpg/960p